  "findings": [
    "Paired Wasmtime speedup is 1.2261049803610888 (MAD 0.044451026865227394) for Quick and 1.248346492262265 (MAD 0.0038123305893742465) for custom hash; public 1.23x/1.25x rounding agrees.",
    "V8 paired Quick 1.0075084239454366 and custom hash 0.9974426187171335 are described as essentially flat; the separate approximately 1 percent hash-only screening loss remains disclosed.",
    "Only warmed Quick (+124 bytes) and custom hash (-13 bytes) change; eight other warmed guests and all ten full example guests are identical. No full-process timing difference is attributed to this compiler change.",
    "Frozen selected native/Wasm reference builds are distinguished from the new paired executions. Profile-specific comparisons are not universal ceilings; CRC outer-repetition AVX2 remains disclosed.",
    "Warmed measurements use native host e046 linked dynamically to Python Wasmtime; process/lifecycle uses e303 linked statically to SDK Wasmtime. Both are 50.0.1 and public prose now distinguishes them.",
    "Recovery retains four exact completed phase records/reports/streams. Old 315-row LangArena child has unknown process exit and zero primary use. Fresh LangArena and lifecycle complete six observed exit-zero phases; cause of original controller termination remains unconfirmed.",
    "Strict live/offline recovery validator binds raw streams, unchanged pins/environment, completion report SHA, exact command differences and timezone-aware chronology. Fourteen identity/state mutations and two timing mutations are rejected.",
    "Current qualification links/counts in Functions and latest runtime section were corrected before this review. Historical comparisons remain explicitly linked to earlier campaigns.",
    "Root visual review is pinned and its current SVG/PNG hashes match; this audit independently verifies proof bindings and numeric/source consistency, not a duplicate visual inspection."
  ],
